<PublicLayout title="Tessellate for agents" description="Use the same resource vocabulary and validated manifests as human editors."><section class="mb-8 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Discover the catalogue</h2><p class="leading-relaxed">Read /data/catalog.json for canonical resource IDs, semantic roles, constraints, dependencies, provenance and licences. Registry JSON at /r/[slug].json contains installable source.</p></section><section class="mb-8 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Compose and mutate</h2><p class="leading-relaxed">The repository CLI and MCP packages compose deterministic manifests and validate mutations against canonical Zod schemas. Read the integration documentation before automating changes.</p></section><section class="mb-8 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Review capability boundary</h2><p class="leading-relaxed">The public site serves discovery files and browser workflows. It does not run a hosted MCP process or present unconfigured API endpoints as functional services.</p></section><p class="flex flex-wrap gap-5"><a class="underline" href="https://github.com/danishgm-sketch/Tessellate">Repository and contributions</a><a class="underline" href="/docs">Documentation</a><a class="underline" href="/explore">Inspect resource licences</a></p><nav class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-5" aria-label="Agent discovery"><a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a><a href="/llms-full.txt">Full catalogue guide</a><a href="/openapi.json">API specification</a><a href="/r/index.json">Registry index</a></nav></PublicLayout>
